Sval: Remove Firefox Relay and the insecure field warning

Firefox Relay's email masks are locked off (Sval spec §10.9), and with
the password manager and address and card autofill gone nothing else
offered them. Relay goes with what only it or those features used: its
form history rows and the sign-up form detection that chose them, its
doorhangers, setting, targeting attributes, glyph, prefs and strings,
the password-saving setting its setting read, the address bar's
password anchor, the insecure password field warning and its row, and
the autocomplete actors' routing of a row's own fill message. Form
history and the login storage stay.

